# 5. Local Search System

Implement a fully local search engine using JavaScript.

The customer can type a question, and B.A.B searches the locally loaded knowledge base.

The search system must work without internet access after the widget and knowledge base have loaded.

## 5.1 Search fields

Search across:
- Question titles.
- Article titles.
- Categories.
- Keywords.
- Synonyms.
- Predefined questions.
- Relevant answer text.

## 5.2 Arabic normalization

Support common Arabic writing variations.

Normalize:
- Remove Arabic diacritics.
- Remove tatweel.
- Normalize أ, إ, and آ to ا.
- Normalize ى to ي.
- Normalize repeated whitespace.
- Ignore unnecessary punctuation.
- Handle common spelling variations through editable synonyms.

Do not apply overly aggressive normalization that could produce misleading results.

## 5.3 Search behavior

Implement:
- Suggestions while typing.
- Search result ranking.
- Keyword matching.
- Synonym matching.
- Partial matching.
- Basic typo tolerance using a lightweight local algorithm.
- A useful no-results state.

Prioritize matches in this order:

1. Exact title or question matches.
2. Keyword and synonym matches.
3. Partial text matches.
4. Broader relevant matches.

Display a limited number of the most relevant results.

When a customer selects a result, show the corresponding predefined answer.

### No-results behavior

If there is no relevant answer, show a friendly Arabic message explaining that the information is not currently available.

Then offer:
- Returning to the main menu.
- Trying a different search.
- Contacting DANDY support through WhatsApp.

Never generate or guess an answer.

